profile: tinyrustlm-mirust.coding-standards.current.v1
updated_utc: 2026-08-28T20:20:00Z

site:
  - Keep the dependency-free PHP, native HTML/CSS, and bounded vanilla-JavaScript architecture.
  - Escape dynamic HTML, preserve semantic and keyboard-accessible routes, and keep content crawlable.
  - Keep current public claims synchronized across PHP, Markdown, llms, UAI, sitemap, release records, and deployment readback.

contracts:
  - Use one clean-slate SLM2 path; delete superseded active readers, aliases, fallbacks, repair, and contradictory prose.
  - Keep MemoryEndpoints.com direct-agent and TinyRustLM.com Connect user-plugin lanes separately identified, authenticated, consented, scoped, provenance-bound, idempotent, and receipted.
  - Treat redundant prelaunch memory as maintained copies: current, secret-safe, provenance-labeled, and noncontradictory.

evidence: Never turn source, tests, configuration, fixtures, mocks, reachability, or package creation into a live capability or publication claim.
